think After landing J7r4 (owner-signed catalog), BUHR's seven journeys have built every named module. Looked for the next plan-exhausted blind spot.
think Grepped: no pond app composes tablecloth with a voice/lantern/query. The intelligence has read the Realidream graph (J6) and pinned corpora (J1), but never a stored artifact by name from Tablecloth. The storage module and the intelligence module stand unjoined — that is the blind spot.
think Self-approved the design round (per the standing autonomous instruction). Named the crux: a voice reads only verified bytes — its corpus is a named artifact fetched through Tablecloth's fetch_artifact, every bead proven by digest and the whole against its recorded address before a byte reaches the voice; a tampered bead refuses the fetch and the voice answers nothing.
think The ground is witnessed: tablecloth.fetch_artifact (J7r1) + the Lantern contract (lantern_core) + graph_query.rye's exact composition shape (route a Lantern prompt to a real reading, metered by max_tokens with a length stop).
obs Ordered the journey: r1 read a named artifact through the verified fetch; r2 track a live publish; r3 gather under the Q-vane host; horizon (owner-signed corpus, Comlink-served) reaches the custody/serve gates.
obs Content-addressed storage becomes the intelligence's integrity guarantee for free — the same verified fetch the store earned, now standing between corpus and reader. That is the Lindy-durable idea this journey is for.
